2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T18:28:13-07:00","id":733600,"title":"","content":"It sounds entirely legitimate.<br /> <br /> It's a <i>terrible</i> idea, given what the Strix are*, but it's entirely legitimate.<br /> <br /> *Demonic owl-spirit-things that want to stop you from playing at being human. Also, can possess you and take you on an atrocity joyride.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T18:28:39-07:00","id":733603,"title":"","content":"Strix don't have bodies?<br /> <br /> Vampires can feed from the mortal bodies and kindred bodies that Strix possess. I don't really see the need for such a merit, or how it'd work, considering the only situation it's sort of applicable is when the Strix uses a Shadow Potency 7 level power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T18:35:19-07:00","id":733610,"title":"","content":"If you had that one &quot;Breath-stealing&quot; power, I could see somebody using it to inhale Strix for Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T19:37:09-07:00","id":733715,"title":"","content":"Personally I would use it as a plot device exclusively because generally that might be a bit too much. In fact, I have used it as a driving plot device to drive a vampire straight up deranged and insane. Remember, Strixes <i>can</i> possess Vampires. In our story a elder vampire had actually diablarized a childe who was possessed, thinking they were going to diablarize him, and thus accidentally took in the Strix. It dropped all his humanity and he went bat shit insane.<br /> <br /> If you want to say &quot;Sure! But it will cost you nearly if not all your humanity, go for it.&quot; It's a dangerous game consuming things like that. So the one way I could see this working is if they hunt down specifically possessed entities and consumed them with the strix within. Which would quickly make them a pariah of the society from the get go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8027-calconstantine","name":"CalConstantine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T00:27:04-07:00","id":734051,"title":"","content":"If you can take it for Ghosts, I suppose you could take it for Strix (pretty sure Ghost is an example?), but have fun combining all the danger of feeding off Werewolves with all the logistical difficulties of feeding off a ghost, what with Strix being ephemeral. Need to find a way to make them manifest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T07:37:29-07:00","id":734677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/733559-unnatural-affinity-for-strix?p=734051#post734051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can take it for Ghosts, I suppose you could take it for Strix (pretty sure Ghost is an example?), but have fun combining all the danger of feeding off Werewolves with all the logistical difficulties of feeding off a ghost, what with Strix being ephemeral. Need to find a way to make them manifest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they're not &quot;ephemeral&quot; <i>per se</i>, they're just not solid. They don't exist in the Twilight state natually, and while they use the simplified Ephemeral Traits, they are still physical objects in the world, being sentient clouds of smoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T12:03:04-07:00","id":735443,"title":"","content":"Edit: What the hell? Why do I have only 1 post, and no avatar? I've been posting on the White Wolf forums for a long time. I'm pretty sure I've been posting here for a while. Was there a recent forum purge?<br /> <br /> Hello, I'm the player of the Strix-embraced vampire. I originally wanted to play a Ventrue Carthian or Invictus, but the DM talked me into playing something more... unique. When he asked me if I was okay with being Embraced by the Strix, I thought that he wanted me to play a Strix-possessed vampire with the memories and personality of my character. He clarified that I would be a normal vampire of the clan of the last vampire the Strix fed from, in this case, Mekhet.<br /> <br /> What happened was that I'm starting play with a BP 6, Humanity 2 Mekhet with no social merits. He was a disenfranchised outcast in life, and he entered death as a super-powered monster who is ignorant of the Traditions or even of his own undead state. First thing he did upon waking up was to contact the police. He just found out that he was supposed to have been dead for two weeks. He doesn't buy it, and believes that he was attacked by a psycho &quot;last night,&quot; and the cops he's talking to are bullshitting him because he's a foreigner (a Korean who moved to the USA to study in college) and they can't be bothered to help some stupid squinty-eyed immigrant.<br /> <br /> Yes, my toon is tearing holes into the Masquerade out of ignorance. He has noticed that he doesn't need to breathe, but with Humanity 2, it doesn't really bother him that much.<br /> <br /> We had a brainstorming session last night with the DM about how the heck I'm going to survive for any length of time in this state. I told him that if my character were completely rational and knowledgeable about the vampiric state, he's go into torpor for 25+ years so he wouldn't have to deal with having to feed on vampires and getting enslaved by the blood bond. We then talked about Unnatural Affinity, and he told me to choose wisely. Possible contenders were: ghosts, werewolves, strix.<br /> <br /> 1. I have no way of interacting with ghosts, so it would be quite tricky to feed from them.<br /> 2. Werewolves, well, I have no problem rerolling, but not so soon after character creation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 3. Strix? He told me that he'd ask Onyx Path, and here we are.<br /> <br /> As for the Strix, I was wondering if it would be a way for my character to enter the All-Night Society as a Strix Detector/Hunter of Owls. My character can taste someone's blood, and if it nourishes him, it must be Strix or vampire blood. We weren't sure if he had a way of telling apart the blood of a normal vampire vs. a Strix-possessed vampire. Presumably, he'd be able to feed on a Strix-possessed mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5187-aron-times","name":"Aron Times","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5187_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T12:54:37-07:00","id":735568,"title":"","content":"Another thing, my character was initially only known as Kenneth, and was named after Kunkka (Kendrick Lim). Kunkka is a Singaporean artist who made a lot of art for DotA, and was so popular that Kunkka the Admiral was named after him. I knew his name began with K, and assumed that it was Kenneth. I only realized a few weeks ago that Kunkka was actually Kendrick and not Kenneth, but I kept the name anyway.<br /> <br /> When he talked to the cops, I made an impromptu decision to make his full name, &quot;Kenneth Jeong.&quot; I realize today that I probably had Ken Jeong in mind, and had subconsciously picked Jeong as his last name because he's an awesome Korean comedian (and doctor). Do you guys have any suggestion for a Korean name? My character is a Korean who is in the USA to study in college, so he wouldn't have been born as Kenneth Jeong; he just adopted the name to sound more native.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5187-aron-times","name":"Aron Times","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5187_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T12:59:15-07:00","id":735573,"title":"","content":"I would probably allow any vampire to develop Unnatural Affinity for the Strix. It'd also be a gateway to a fate worse than Final Death, of course. Most Strix would probably encourage it, welcome it, when the vampire began feeding, and the act would bring with it the rush of diablerie. Its power, too, as the vampire grows stronger with each Strix he or she devours. Yet as the vampire consumes Striges, the Beast grows stronger, more ferocious, ever hungrier. The vampire's eyes become overlarge and sickly yellow, skin pale as snow, nose and mouth slowly merging together into a bone-white beak. At the peak of its power, Humanity is gone, long since consumed by the Beast. Its Blood Potency hits 10 and now it is a creature of blood and smoke, both of which wreathe it in an evil aura. When it opens its beak, it cries out with the damned voice of the Beast\u2014and the malevolent wail of every Strix the vampire devoured. This is the Beast made manifest, and it is hungry.<br /> <br /> <i>Run</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T13:20:26-07:00","id":735633,"title":"","content":"If a strix detector is part of the story then I would just give him the unique merit Unseen Sense: Strix. The short hairs on the back of his neck would alert him to the presence of a strix, but not necessarily who in the room it was possessing. It could also lead to some interesting times if the covenants found out about him, with the Dragons wanting to study him, the Sanctified wanting to use him for hunting and the Crone wanting to read his entrails or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T15:43:22-07:00","id":736035,"title":"","content":"That's weird, i always assumed that if a Kindred is physically able to drink from a Strix, he would be able to get sustenance from it. Since Strigis explicitly have Vitae and turn blood into Vitae when they feed, i thought it would make sense that Kindred that can only be sustained by Kindred Vitae could use Vitae from a Strix as well since there doesn't seem to be any difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2213,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","user":"TittoPaolo210","date":". 10-28-2015, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T16:09:31-07:00","id":736110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TittoPaolo210</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/733559-unnatural-affinity-for-strix?p=736035#post736035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's weird, i always assumed that if a Kindred is physically able to drink from a Strix, he would be able to get sustenance from it. Since Strigis explicitly have Vitae and turn blood into Vitae when they feed,</div> </div> </div> </div>Strix don't feed on blood, they feed on breath, taking their Vitae from there. It suffuses their shadow-bodies, which isn't the same as carrying it in a blood medium.<br /> <br /> Now, when the Strix has a body, that body has blood, and you can feed from that. A Strix possessing a Kindred has that Kindred's Vitae in their body, which you can theoretically drink. I don't believe you'll actually be able to drink from the Strix's Vitae pool, however.<br /> <br /> Which goes back to what I said before. Strix don't have blood or bodies, so vampires can't drink from them. MAYBE they could when a Strix Materializes, but that requires a Shadow Potency of 6-7 which is not gonna be all that common.<br /> <br /> Compare ghosts, who can actually have an easier time manifesting than Strix do. It's no wonder they're a potential target for the Unnatural Affinity merit, precisely because all they need is the Materialize Manifestation for Kindred to potentially feed from them.<br /> <br /> Most of the time when you could feed from the Strix, you're feeding from the body it inhabits, which sort of obviates the unnatural affinity issue. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T17:08:10-07:00","id":736284,"title":"","content":"Counting a living strix-possessed human as a supernatural being could be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:09:51-07:00","id":736417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/733559-unnatural-affinity-for-strix?p=736110#post736110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Strix don't feed on blood, they feed on breath, taking their Vitae from there. It suffuses their shadow-bodies, which isn't the same as carrying it in a blood medium.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, i intended to say life-force, but in any case the rest of your post makes perfect sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T19:36:06-07:00","id":736554,"title":"","content":"Unless I'm wrong about how Unnatural Affinity works, it only provides another type of creature the vampire can feed on that counts as Kindred for feeding restrictions. It does not remove the ability to feed on Kindred.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Strix, given the dangers involved in this type of prey I am inclined to be generous with how to feed on them. At the very least, (attempting) feeding on anyone possessed by Strix would work, corpse, revenant or human.<br /> Given the fluff, namely how the Strix are <b><i>physical shadows </i></b>and have <i><b>vitae distributed</b></i> <i><b>through out</b></i> their bodies, that they feed on breath and they can tear each other apart to devour one another...I'm also willing to take it a step further. I'd say that Unnatural Affinity: Strix let's you consume the Birds of Dis in the normal Shadow Form, provided you can keep it from running away. You might not need to breath or grasp the darkness, but you can inhale smoke* if you choose too.<br /> <br /> Just beware; I'd rule the Kiss doesn't apply so there is nothing stopping the Owl from trying to take control of your body.<br /> <br /> <br /> *yes the strix aren't literal smoke, it's poetic license.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T20:21:12-07:00","id":736657,"title":"","content":"Ah well, the point is moot, as the DM and I have decided that it's too much trouble. Instead, Kenneth Jeong has Natural Affinity: Werewolves.<br /> <br /> This is going to be a fun (and short) Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5187-aron-times","name":"Aron Times","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5187_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T00:25:57-07:00","id":737246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aron Times</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/733559-unnatural-affinity-for-strix?p=735443#post735443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: What the hell? Why do I have only 1 post, and no avatar? I've been posting on the White Wolf forums for a long time. I'm pretty sure I've been posting here for a while. Was there a recent forum purge?<br /> <br /> Hello, I'm the player of the Strix-embraced vampire. I originally wanted to play a Ventrue Carthian or Invictus, but the DM talked me into playing something more... unique. When he asked me if I was okay with being Embraced by the Strix, I thought that he wanted me to play a Strix-possessed vampire with the memories and personality of my character. He clarified that I would be a normal vampire of the clan of the last vampire the Strix fed from, in this case, Mekhet.<br /> <br /> What happened was that I'm starting play with a BP 6, Humanity 2 Mekhet with no social merits. He was a disenfranchised outcast in life, and he entered death as a super-powered monster who is ignorant of the Traditions or even of his own undead state. First thing he did upon waking up was to contact the police. He just found out that he was supposed to have been dead for two weeks. He doesn't buy it, and believes that he was attacked by a psycho &quot;last night,&quot; and the cops he's talking to are bullshitting him because he's a foreigner (a Korean who moved to the USA to study in college) and they can't be bothered to help some stupid squinty-eyed immigrant.<br /> <br /> Yes, my toon is tearing holes into the Masquerade out of ignorance. He has noticed that he doesn't need to breathe, but with Humanity 2, it doesn't really bother him that much.<br /> <br /> We had a brainstorming session last night with the DM about how the heck I'm going to survive for any length of time in this state. I told him that if my character were completely rational and knowledgeable about the vampiric state, he's go into torpor for 25+ years so he wouldn't have to deal with having to feed on vampires and getting enslaved by the blood bond. We then talked about Unnatural Affinity, and he told me to choose wisely. Possible contenders were: ghosts, werewolves, strix.<br /> <br /> 1. I have no way of interacting with ghosts, so it would be quite tricky to feed from them.<br /> 2. Werewolves, well, I have no problem rerolling, but not so soon after character creation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 3. Strix? He told me that he'd ask Onyx Path, and here we are.<br /> <br /> As for the Strix, I was wondering if it would be a way for my character to enter the All-Night Society as a Strix Detector/Hunter of Owls. My character can taste someone's blood, and if it nourishes him, it must be Strix or vampire blood. We weren't sure if he had a way of telling apart the blood of a normal vampire vs. a Strix-possessed vampire. Presumably, he'd be able to feed on a Strix-possessed mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless you're trying to handicap yourself and push the rules to the breaking limit, I'd question the decision making here. The high BP, low humanity, and feeding restriction on their own would make playing a starting level character difficult, but combine those together and it's going to be a mess.<br /> <br /> He's two steps away from being a mindless monster, and even passing as human is going to be difficult given that restriction. That means sinking vitae, which is already a valuable commodity for your guy, into any attempts at social interaction. As a neonate, he doesn't really have the political leverage to arrange for feeding off other kindred, and unless he sets up some sort of symbiotic relationship with a werewolf, he's going to die. quickly. At humanity 2 with no built-in social network, even interacting with other kindred is going to be a hot mess.That combination of traits means he's going to be isolated both from humanity and other kindred. Even if he doesn't get ripped to shreds trying to feed off a lupine, he's going to lose his humanity pretty damn quickly.<br /> <br /> Good luck! I'm curious to see how it plays out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:24:50-07:00","id":739456,"title":"","content":"oh as I backed the kickstarter... how good an idea would unnatural affinity beast be? For a fledgling with a ridiculously high BP Because he was embraced by a strix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:42:58-07:00","id":739521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/733559-unnatural-affinity-for-strix?p=739456#post739456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh as I backed the kickstarter... how good an idea would unnatural affinity beast be? For a fledgling with a ridiculously high BP Because he was embraced by a strix.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he can get a Beast friend, not a bad idea at all. Hunting beasts? Not a great idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:57:16-07:00","id":739554,"title":"","content":"Ok, maybe I missed something, but why does this neonate have really high blood potency? Synthesis can only raise the potency of pre-existing vampires. Anything else just gets blood potency 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T18:06:10-07:00","id":740365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/733559-unnatural-affinity-for-strix?p=739554#post739554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, maybe I missed something, but why does this neonate have really high blood potency? Synthesis can only raise the potency of pre-existing vampires. Anything else just gets blood potency 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>His game, his rules. I didn't think it was legal, but hey, DM prerogative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5187-aron-times","name":"Aron Times","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5187_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T05:08:47-07:00","id":741391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/733559-unnatural-affinity-for-strix?p=735573#post735573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would probably allow any vampire to develop Unnatural Affinity for the Strix. It'd also be a gateway to a fate worse than Final Death, of course. Most Strix would probably encourage it, welcome it, when the vampire began feeding, and the act would bring with it the rush of diablerie. Its power, too, as the vampire grows stronger with each Strix he or she devours. Yet as the vampire consumes Striges, the Beast grows stronger, more ferocious, ever hungrier. The vampire's eyes become overlarge and sickly yellow, skin pale as snow, nose and mouth slowly merging together into a bone-white beak. At the peak of its power, Humanity is gone, long since consumed by the Beast. Its Blood Potency hits 10 and now it is a creature of blood and smoke, both of which wreathe it in an evil aura. When it opens its beak, it cries out with the damned voice of the Beast\u2014and the malevolent wail of every Strix the vampire devoured. This is the Beast made manifest, and it is hungry.<br /> <br /> <i>Run</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;The Call of the Void, Mr Murdock.&quot; The therapist clicked his lips as the words flowed out. &quot;Tell me more about this concept.&quot;<br /> <br /> Murdock rose to speak but as his voice started to form, words of various sinister construction fell out from him. He retched over, blood falling freely out of his mouth as vomit hit the floor. His mouth continued it's motion. Speaking a thousand harsh concepts.<br /> <br /> The Therapist flashed his optics. His face unmoved. &quot;Ah. Most intriguing I must say. Seeing as you are currently incapacitated in this manner, I found it prudent to do such research on my own behalf on the subject. I dearly wish to hear your side of the concept, giving your present condition as a case study, but it stands to reason that is such a thing as sticking your hand too far into the fire.&quot;<br /> <br /> Murdock fell on all fours, the voices coursing and pulsing through his brain like writhing larva of some insidious parasite. He struggled to remain lucid. He grasped the islands of the mind.<br /> <br /> &quot;Call of the void is the social phenomenon of which one has the thought of engaging in harmful actions against another or even one's self. The thought of holding a knife and the fleeting thought of stabbing a friend. The impulse of driving a car and slamming it head on onto another while driving. Such a puzzling thing to be included into human nature.&quot; The Therapist folded his hands together. &quot;Don't you agree Mr Murdock?&quot;<br /> <br /> Murdock continued to vomit, his vision swarmed. Shadows danced around his eyes and inner demons laughed in his ears.<br /> <br /> &quot;I must say, given your present condition, could you perhaps enlighten me on how this... situation came to be?&quot;<br /> <br /> Murdock's body went limp as his mind called forth events. With raspy voices composed of talons and blood, they spoke. They spoke of the glee of which they killed, murdered and allowed themselves to be murdered. They spoke of the toy-men which they broke and delighted in their fear of the hunt. They spoke of the families shattered, and parliaments dissolved. They spoke of structures long dead and buried awakened only for the pure amusement of being slain again. They spoke with laughter of the never dead.<br /> <br /> The Therapist tapped his pen, his notes long compiled. For a long while, there was silence.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thank you Mr Murdock. That was quite enlightening.&quot; He slowly turned away, leaving Murdock to arise in a quite unfamiliar place. A place with no doors and only a slight heavily barred window. Red horizon covered the sky as leering creatures walked past and occasionally tapped on the glass. Panic within him rose and for once, all the voices shared the same fear.<br /> <br /> &quot;You see, Mr Murdock, You are quite the case study. We can't have you running wild to... degenerate nor shall we need you to self repair. you shall be kept as an example as your kind. A lesson for the Analysts to practice on. We are quite thankful for your kind's ability for stasis. Quite wonderful to work with a blank slate.&quot;<br /> <br /> Murdock panicked. He tore at the walls. He screamed at the window. He followed every suggestion that his insane mind and soul could come up with. Finally, he wept.<br /> <br /> &quot;Until next time, Mr Murdock.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T15:42:18-07:00","id":743083,"title":"","content":"Very nice! It serves to illustrate that vampires and Strix do not mix\u2014like oil and blood. Or smoke and blood, rather.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T16:02:23-07:00","id":743143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/733559-unnatural-affinity-for-strix?p=739521#post739521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he can get a Beast friend, not a bad idea at all. Hunting beasts? Not a great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div> Or third option, get a beast buddy to help you hunt other beasts, so the beast can feed too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T16:31:43-07:00","id":743205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/733559-unnatural-affinity-for-strix?p=743083#post743083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very nice! It serves to illustrate that vampires and Strix do not mix\u2014like oil and blood. Or smoke and blood, rather.</div> </div> </div> </div>They actually mix quite well. The issue at hand though is that it's a non-stop train to the Beast and the extinction of you the human. Some would say the kindred could do if they would stop being such little children and live up to their potential. Just like the Strix want them to. Just as Planned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T00:00:06-07:00","id":745993,"title":"","content":"Speaking of synthesis and weird ties and associations - would a vampire created through that power feel any sort of blood sympathy toward another kindred or revenant spawned years or decades later by the same strix?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T01:10:53-08:00","id":746144,"title":"","content":"I think so. Certainly the Baron's childer have blood ties as kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T06:56:24-08:00","id":749085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/733559-unnatural-affinity-for-strix?p=746144#post746144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think so. Certainly the Baron's childer have blood ties as kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Baron? Which NPC is this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T07:56:35-08:00","id":749177,"title":"","content":"A strix that has been controlling a vampire named Baron \u00d6rnsk\u00f6ld for most of his requiem. He's on page 214 of VtR 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}